{"content":[{"c":["ABEL-MEHOLAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Birthplace of the prophet Elisha (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.16","r":"1Kgs.19.16","rawR":"1Kgs.19.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.16","value":"1Kgs.19.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:16"},"). Here Elijah found Elisha plowing and threw his coat over Elisha’s shoulders, symbolizing God’s call to Elisha to become a prophet (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.19-21","r":"1Kgs.19.19-21","rawR":"1Kgs.19.19-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.19-21","value":"1Kgs.19.19-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:19-21"},"). The town is earlier mentioned as one place to which the Midianites fled from Gideon’s 300 warriors (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.7.22","r":"Judg.7.22","rawR":"Judg.7.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.7.22","value":"Judg.7.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 7:22"},"). It is also mentioned in a list of administrative districts set up by King Solomon (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.12","r":"1Kgs.4.12","rawR":"1Kgs.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.12","value":"1Kgs.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:12"},"). The most likely modern identification is Khirbet Tell el-Hilu."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AbelMeholah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 19:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.19.16","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.19.16","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.19.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 19:19-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.19.19-21","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.19.19-21","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.19.19-21"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 7:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.7.22","rawQueryValue":"Judg.7.22","sourceRefExact":"Judg.7.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.12","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.12","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6f62af78f8d3d01a3e4fa485413bcd6fda765439d803b630fdad8d219124e1fb","sourceItemName":"AbelMeholah","sourceItemOrder":22,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AbelMeholah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Abel-Meholah","title":"Abel-Meholah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}